# The corpus grows as the fuzzer runs; only the checked-in seeds are tracked.
#
# `!*/` rather than a named directory: `*` excludes the per-harness directories
# themselves, and git will not look inside an excluded directory, so a `.seed`
# under one that is not re-included is invisible - `git status` stays clean and
# the fixture is silently absent. This rule named `pattern/` alone, which was
# the only harness that had seeds, so the same file under `crossengine/` or
# `subject/` was dropped. Re-including every directory instead means a fourth
# harness does not have to remember to amend this file.
*
!.gitignore
!*/
!*.seed
